            "review_title": "Review at Hangang Korean Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Glenn C\nWilmington, North Carolina51 contributions\n0\nWho's Watching The Kitchen?\nJun 2013 • Solo\nWho's watching the kitchen? This is my question about this restaurant. This is a mom and pop restaurant evidenced by appearance, food preparation, and presentation. I lived in Korea for about a year. This restaurant represents Korean food from the countryside of Korea. The food is not very tasty, not well prepared, and not inviting. I guess I am slightly bias because I too cook Korean food and that very good.. \n\nKorean food is some of the best food in all the world when cooked and prepared correct. This restaurant has no ambiance, no feeling, and lacks any type of culinary sophistication. It is embrassing when located in a major city, an a major business district. There are numerous Korean restaurants located the next street over on Thai Van Lung which has far more to offer quality and price wise than this restaurant.\n\nWhen I arrived at the restaurant it was mid afternoon. I was greeted by Vietnamese servers with sad looks on their faces. I should have took the obvious warning. I ordered baby clam miso soup with the baby clams were missing and served luke warm with panchan (Korean side dishes) included pancake which was horrible and no taste. It seem as if I was eating paper when I bit into the pancakes. \n\n The kimchi was definitely not the very best; I have eaten kimchi at Japanese reataurants which are better. For an entreee, I ordered Steam Short Fish which translated is \"Mackeral in a box\" and that's exactly what it tasted like. The menu highlighted fresh fish cooked in a kimchi sauce. This recipe was far from that. They served me dry fish overcooked in kimchi sauce. Deceptive advertising the dish did not look like the picture portrayed in the menu.\n\nThis restaurant prices were extremely expensive the lowest price item was 100,000 VND/$5.00 USD and the highest price item was 370,000 VND/$16.00 USD. For lunch time most local restaurants lowered their prices to attract the lunch crowd, but not here. The restaurant is located in a dingy second floor building and very small to say the least. I really don't know why anyone would rate this restaurant excellent except they have never been to a good Korean restaurant. There are a lot of good Korean restaurants in Ho Chi Minh City; this is not one of them.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 5, 2013",
