            "review_title": "Review at Hangang Korean Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Gary_TO_12\nToronto, Canada170 contributions\n1\nExcellent Korean Restaurant in Saigon\nJan 2013 • Couples\nWe have generally been disappointed with Korean restaurants outside of Korea in Asia (i.e. Hong Kong and China), but Hangang was the exception to this rule.\nThis is a Korean run restaurant and the food is real home cooking.\nThe panchan (small dishes) is fresh and of a good variety, the kimchi is home-made and the chigaes hot, excellent tasting and full of fresh ingredients (I tried both the Kimchi Chigae and the Donjang Chigae and my wife tried the Chungookchung Chigae. The fish dish was also exceptional (we had a pan fried fish dish- local fish).\nThe owner is generous with the air conditioning (something important in Saigon!)\nNot fancy decor, but a basic, well run family restaurant with excellent food and value for money.\nThe real proof of authenticity is that each time we went there, everyone eating there was Korean (except for us!)\nThe restaurant is located across the street from the Northern Hotel and is on the 2nd floor up a staircase from the street.\nThey provided us with a picture menu with items described in English.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten February 3, 2013",
